<% content_for :title, "Why Janela is called Janela" %>

<section class="name-hero">
  <span class="hero-mark-wrap" data-controller="fan" data-action="mouseenter->fan#shuffle">
    <%= render "shared/logo", size: 150, class_name: "hero-mark" %>
  </span>
  <p class="name-word">ja·ne·la</p>
  <p class="name-gloss"><em>noun, Portuguese.</em> A window.</p>
  <p class="lede name-lede">
    Every name in this library was chosen on purpose, and a few were changed after they shipped.
    The idea underneath all of them is that your application keeps its own words.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="anatomy">
  <h2>The anatomy of a window</h2>
  <p class="lede">
    Once the library is a window, the rest of the vocabulary follows from the thing itself rather
    than from a list of synonyms for chart.
  </p>

  <div class="anatomy-parts vitral-panes">
    <div class="anatomy-part vitral-pane">
      <p class="anatomy-term">Janela</p>
      <p class="anatomy-means">the library</p>
      <p>A window onto your data. Uncommon in English, obvious once explained.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="anatomy-part vitral-pane">
      <p class="anatomy-term">Frame</p>
      <p class="anatomy-means">a dashboard</p>
      <p>What holds the panes. A name and a grid, and nothing your users have to see.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="anatomy-part vitral-pane">
      <p class="anatomy-term">Pane</p>
      <p class="anatomy-means">one visual</p>
      <p>A pane of glass in the frame. Each one looks through at part of the picture.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="anatomy-part vitral-pane">
      <p class="anatomy-term">Vitral</p>
      <p class="anatomy-means">the theme</p>
      <p>A stained glass window. Colour held in each pane, lead between them, light from behind.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="anatomy-part vitral-pane">
      <p class="anatomy-term">Grid</p>
      <p class="anatomy-means">the layout</p>
      <p>How a frame is divided: its columns, the gap between panes, and how wide each one sits.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<section class="name-rule">
  <blockquote>
    Uncommon but understandable, conceivable words, so that people aren't pigeonholed and can
    select their own nomenclature.
  </blockquote>
  <p class="lede">
    A library that calls its main idea a Dashboard has taken that word from every application that
    installs it. Janela's words sit a step to the side, so they never collide with yours, and your
    users read whatever you call things in your own locale file.
  </p>
</section>

<section class="name-story">
  <div class="doc-prose vitral-pane"><%= @doc.html %></div>
  <%# No "this page as a guide" link beside it any more: that guide is this
      page, and the link pointed at a URL that now redirects back here. %>
  <p class="doc-crumb doc-crumb-end">
    <a href="https://github.com/retail-tasker/janela/blob/main/docs/naming.md">In the repository</a>
  </p>
</section>
